{"name":"Banana Crepe","hex":"#e7d3ad","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"banana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The elongated curved tropical fruit of a banana plant, which grows in bunches and has a creamy flesh and a smooth skin. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","In particular, the sweet, yellow fruit of the Cavendish banana cultivar, which may be eaten raw, as distinct from e.g. a plantain for cooking."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Curved like a banana, especially of a ball in flight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana"},{"term":"crepe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat round pancake-like pastry from Lower Brittany, made with wheat.","A soft thin light fabric with a crinkled surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover in crepe.","To crease (paper) in such a way to make it look like crepe paper"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crepe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Banana","blocks":[{"text":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg/330px-Bananavarieties.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","wikidata":"Q503"},{"title":"Crêpe","blocks":[{"text":"A crêpe is a dish made from unleavened batter or dough that is cooked on a frying pan or a griddle. Crêpes are usually one of two varieties: sweet crêpes or savoury crêpes. They are often served with a wide variety of fillings such as cheese, fruit, vegetables, meats, and a variety of spreads. Crêpes can also be flambéed, such as in Crêpes Suzette."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Crepes_dsc07085.jpg/330px-Crepes_dsc07085.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cr%C3%AApe","wikidata":"Q12200"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Banana_corm.jpg/250px-Banana_corm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Banana_corm.jpg/330px-Banana_corm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Banana_corm.jpg/250px-Banana_corm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABanana_corm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Young_Banana_Sapling_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3447.jpg/120px-Young_Banana_Sapling_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3447.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Young_Banana_Sapling_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3447.jpg/250px-Young_Banana_Sapling_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3447.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Young_Banana_Sapling_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3447.jpg/120px-Young_Banana_Sapling_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3447.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoung_Banana_Sapling_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3447.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi